---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Terms of Use';
const description = 'The terms governing use of worldbatteryhub.com: permitted use, citation and attribution, intellectual property, automated access, warranty and liability.';
const canonical = '/terms-of-use/';

const jsonLd = [{
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Terms of Use',
  description,
  url: 'https://worldbatteryhub.com/terms-of-use/',
}];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  ogType="article"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  dateModified="2026-09-21"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="byline">Legal · Last reviewed 2026-09-21</p>
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        These terms govern your use of <strong>worldbatteryhub.com</strong> and its sub-sites. By accessing or
        using the site you accept them. If you do not accept them, please do not use the site.
      </p>

      <div class="takeaways">
        <strong>At a glance:</strong> Read, learn and quote us freely — with attribution. Do not republish the
        platform wholesale, do not present our figures as certified laboratory or manufacturer test results,
        and do not misrepresent your relationship with us. Automated access for indexing and research is
        welcome at reasonable rates; abusive scraping is not.
      </div>

      <h2>1. Purpose of this website</h2>
      <p>
        World Battery Hub publishes battery knowledge and data: technology explanations, specifications,
        comparison tables, calculators, glossary entries, testing and standards references, manufacturer and
        market information, and related content for engineers, buyers, students and researchers.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where a sub-site is operated on a separate domain (for example our data, technology, testing,
        manufacturer or market sub-sites), these terms apply to it unless that sub-site publishes its own
        terms.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Permitted use</h2>
      <p>You may:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>read, browse and print pages for your own internal, professional or educational use;</li>
        <li>quote, excerpt or summarise our content — including in reports, articles, specifications and
            presentations — provided you attribute World Battery Hub as the source and, where practical, link
            to the page you used;</li>
        <li>use our published figures with the source and any confidence label intact;</li>
        <li>link to any page of this platform.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Prohibited use</h2>
      <p>You may not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>republish, resell, mirror or redistribute substantial parts of this platform, or offer it as a
            substitute for accessing it (including in a paid database or behind a login);</li>
        <li>remove, obscure or alter source attributions, confidence labels, review dates or copyright notices;</li>
        <li>present our content, figures or data as certified laboratory results, manufacturer test data,
            regulatory approval, or your own original research;</li>
        <li>state or imply that World Battery Hub endorses, certifies, partners with or audits you, your
            products or your services, without our prior written agreement;</li>
        <li>use automated means to access the site in a way that imposes an unreasonable load, circumvents
            access controls, or extracts the platform in bulk for republication;</li>
        <li>use the site for any unlawful, misleading, defamatory or infringing purpose, or in a way that
            interferes with other users' access.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Automated access, indexing and AI systems</h2>
      <p>
        Search-engine indexing and normal, rate-limited automated access for research and citation are
        welcome. Bulk extraction for republication, or automated access that degrades the service, is not —
        and we may rate-limit, block or require an agreement for such access.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where you cite or summarise our content in machine-generated output, the same attribution
        requirements in section 2 apply: credit World Battery Hub and link to the source page. Do not present
        our compiled data as authoritative physical measurements, and do not drop confidence labels where we
        provide them.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        This platform's content — explanatory text, comparison tables, calculators, compiled datasets,
        structure, design and code — is owned by or licensed to the operator of World Battery Hub and is
        protected by applicable intellectual property law. "World Battery Hub" and the platform's visual
        identity are our marks. Third-party standards, product names, company names and trademarks remain the
        property of their respective owners.
      </p>
      <p>
        You receive no licence beyond the permitted use in section 2. For commercial republishing,
        integration or data-licensing enquiries, contact
        <a href="mailto:data@worldbatteryhub.com">data@worldbatteryhub.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Content accuracy, corrections and change</h2>
      <p>
        Our research and correction process is described in <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a> and the
        limits of what we claim are stated in our <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>. We may add, correct,
        restructure or withdraw content at any time. Figures published by third parties — including
        manufacturers and market research — may change after we publish, and a page's review date reflects our
        last check, not the third party's.
      </p>

      <h2>7. No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The platform is provided <strong>"as is" and "as available"</strong>, without warranty of any kind,
        express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, completeness, timeliness,
        availability or non-infringement. We do not warrant that the site will be uninterrupted, secure or
        free of errors, or that any figure is suitable for your specific application.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, the operator of World Battery Hub is not liable for
        any direct, indirect, incidental, consequential, special or punitive loss arising from your use of, or
        reliance on, this platform or its content — including loss of profit, business, data or goodwill,
        equipment or property damage, personal injury, or the cost of substitute information or services.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where liability cannot lawfully be excluded, our aggregate liability is limited to the greater of
        (a) the amount you paid us for the content or service giving rise to the claim, or (b) one hundred
        US dollars.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Availability and changes to the platform</h2>
      <p>
        We may change, suspend or withdraw any part of the platform — including sub-sites, tools and datasets —
        at any time and without notice, and we do not guarantee that any URL will remain available or that
        content will be retained.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Governing law and disputes</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the People's Republic of China. The parties will first attempt
        to resolve any dispute through good-faith negotiation in writing; failing that, the dispute is subject
        to the jurisdiction of the competent courts at the operator's place of establishment in China. Nothing
        in these terms limits any mandatory consumer-protection right you may have where you live.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. The version published on this page, with the review date
        above, governs your use of the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Related policies</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> — the limits of what we claim.</li>
        <li><a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> — what we collect and why.</li>
        <li><a href="/safety-notice/">Safety &amp; Liability Notice</a> — battery hazards.</li>
        <li><a href="/data-use-and-citation/">Data Use &amp; Citation</a> — reuse and citation terms.</li>
        <li><a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a> — how content is researched and corrected.</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="muted">
        Questions about these terms? Email
        <a href="mailto:editorial@worldbatteryhub.com">editorial@worldbatteryhub.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
